.TH AVR\-AUDIT\-EVENTS\-LIST 1 "" "avr 0.1.4" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-audit-events-list \- List audit events for the organization.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr audit-events list
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
List audit events for the organization.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    acting_api_key_id, action, actor_type, actor_user_id, client_ip,
    created_at, event_data, event_id, resource_id, resource_type
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-resource\-type\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter by resource type (e.g. api_key, user).
.TP
\fB\-\-action\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter by action (CREATE, UPDATE, DELETE, ...).
.TP
\fB\-\-actor\-user\-id\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter by acting user id.
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR, \fB\-\-created\-after\fR \fITEXT\fR
ISO-8601 lower bound (inclusive) on created_at.
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR, \fB\-\-created\-before\fR \fITEXT\fR
ISO-8601 upper bound (exclusive) on created_at.
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-limit\fR \fIINTEGER RANGE\fR
Max events to return. (default: 100)
.TP
\fB\-\-cursor\fR \fITEXT\fR
Opaque cursor from a previous response's next_cursor.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-audit-events (1)
